  (text "VREF = 2.495 V from TL431 (U603). C601 must be 10 uF: a TL431 can oscillate with 10 nF - 3 uF on its output."
    (at 25 246.0 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.27 1.27))
      (justify left top))
    (uuid 1ec89f2d-6712-413c-bf90-aa294fef2967))
  (text "Six trips pull FAULT_N low (open-collector, wired-OR): OV cell > 4.33 V | UV cell < 1.96 V | discharge > 11.6 A | charge > 6.2 A | heatsink or cell NTC > about 62 C."
    (at 25 250.5 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.27 1.27))
      (justify left top))
    (uuid 9ceb672b-729a-416b-bd96-44bfabfa6919))
  (text "Latch (U602C): once FAULT_N has been low for about 1 ms it is held low. The MCU re-arms by driving ARM (PB10) high for a moment, and can force a trip by driving ARM low. Normally ARM is high-Z."
    (at 25 255.0 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.27 1.27))
      (justify left top))
    (uuid e8a63269-d0b8-4281-bfa1-d6dbc15b566c))
  (text "Power-up state is \"tripped\": FAULT_N low, K4 off, +12V_SW dead, load off. Nothing moves until the firmware arms the bench. No USB (no +3V3) also means tripped."
    (at 25 259.5 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.27 1.27))
      (justify left top))
    (uuid eb59128d-7871-4a15-9b14-6b05e609bdea))
  (text "U602D turns FAULT_N into SW_B, which drives the safety switch K4 (Power sheet). UV also trips with no cell inserted."
    (at 25 264.0 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.27 1.27))
      (justify left top))
    (uuid 406dac2d-4115-4737-9352-bfd347dc11f1))
  (text "How it works / what to check: docs/SCHEMATIC_GUIDE.md section 6."
    (at 25 268.5 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.27 1.27))
      (justify left top))
    (uuid d88304d7-6008-4be9-bc8b-f33695960b34)))
